  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To effectively contribute to national development and foster resilient labour markets, it is imperative to strengthen the institutional and operational capacities of employers&#x2019; organizations in Indonesia, particularly APINDO, KADIN, and relevant sectoral entities, such as in garment, fishing, palm oil and electronics. These organizations have become increasingly engaged in shaping labour, employment, and investment policies, yet they continue to face systemic challenges in service delivery, coordination, and policy influence. A recent milestone in this regard is APINDO&#x2019;s submission of an economic roadmap to the government, intended to inform the 2025&#x2013;2029 Medium-Term Development Plan. This initiative represents a positive step forward, but ongoing monitoring and engagement will be necessary to ensure its successful integration and implementation.
Under this outcome, a strategic approach would prioritize governance and services and enhancing collaboration mechanisms to prevent overlap and fragmentation. Employers&#x2019; organizations must also professionalize their policy engagement processes through the timely production and dissemination of evidence-based policy briefs and economic roadmaps. This includes forging stronger partnerships with academic and research institutions to reinforce the credibility and impact of their policy proposals. Furthermore, embedding digital tools and platforms for real-time policy tracking, stakeholder communication, and coordinated advocacy will significantly enhance responsiveness and outreach. A targeted focus on sustained engagement with government stakeholders and media, supported by robust monitoring and evaluation systems, will ensure that strategic contributions from the business community are effectively integrated into Indonesia&#x2019;s labour and development policies.</narrative>
  </description>
